,"target_quote":"","line":65,"k":2,"unit_id":"DDC-053-5-1-2-199b0bc1","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":5,"target_pdf_page":63,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-053","src_page":"5","text":"App. A ¶¶ 76, 185, 304–306","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-051-13","target_page":"103","target_page_end":"105","target_pin":"¶¶ 304–306","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":66,"k":3,"unit_id":"DDC-053-5-1-3-199b0bc1","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":5,"target_pdf_page":103,"target_pdf_page_end":105,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-053","src_page":"5","text":"A-9","n":"1","kind":"exhibit-usb","target_doc":"USB-A-9","target_page":"1","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"A-9","status":"mapped","target_quote":"","line":67,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-053-5-1-1-7f5d69d0","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":5,"target_pdf_page":1,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-053","src_page":"5","text":"A-12","n":"1","kind":"exhibit-usb","target_doc":"USB-A-12","target_page":"1","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"A-12","status":"mapped","target_quote":"","line":68,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-053-5-1-1-6766e3e7","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":5,"target_pdf_page":1,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-053","src_page":"5","text":"Notice of Errata § II.A","n":"2","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-052","target_page":"3","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"§ II.A","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":69,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-053-5-2-1-249b41db","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":5,"target_pdf_page":3,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-053","src_page":"6","text":"LCvR 5.4(e)(1)","n":"1","kind":"rule","target_doc":"Local Rules AUG_2025","target_page":"27","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"LCvR 5.4(e)(1)","status":"verified","target_quote":"(1) Every unsealed document (including an administrative record or a record of state court proceedings) must be filed electronically. Every document filed under seal in a totally sealed case shall be filed in paper form accompanied by an electronic copy in a format deemed compatible by the Clerk's Office with CM/ECF filing in conformity with the requirements of LCvR 5.1. Any document, exhibit, or attachment, including sealed material that (A) is not in a format that readily permits electronic filing, such as a map, chart or DVD, or (B) is illegible when scanned into electronic format, is to be maintained in the possession of the attorney or pro se party responsible for the filing. Such a filing shall be made available for a party or the Court and must be identified in a Notice of Filing filed with the Court. A document or item filed pursuant to this subsection shall be served, if it is necessary to serve it, by mail or by hand delivery, unless the parties have otherwise agreed.","line":70,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-053-6-1-1-69eed61e","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":6,"target_pdf_page":27,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-053","src_page":"6","text":"Section V and Appendix A","n":"1","kind":"internal","target_doc":"DDC-053","target_page":"4","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"Section V","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":71,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-053-6-1-1-1e6fd9b3","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":6,"target_pdf_page":4,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-053","src_page":"6","text":"Section V and Appendix A","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-053-01","target_page":"1","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"Appendix A (ECF 53-1)","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":72,"k":2,"unit_id":"DDC-053-6-1-2-1e6fd9b3","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":6,"target_pdf_page":1,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-053","src_page":"6","text":"FRE 902(11)","n":"1","kind":"rule","target_doc":"Federal Rules of Evidence (Dec. 1, 2025, uscourts.gov official pamphlet)","target_page":"26","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"Rule 902(11)","status":"verified","target_quote":"(11) Certified Domestic Records of a Regularly Conducted Activity. The original or a copy of a domestic record that meets the requirements of Rule 803(6)(A)-(C), as shown by a certification of the custodian or another qualified person that complies with a federal statute or a rule prescribed by the Supreme Court. Before the trial or hearing, the proponent must give an adverse party reasonable written notice of the intent to offer the record-and must make the record and certification available for inspection-so that the party has a fair opportunity to challenge them.","line":73,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-053-6-1-1-f54ac262","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":6,"target_pdf_page":41,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-053","src_page":"6","text":"Compl. ¶¶ 48, 57","n":"1","kind":"tac","target_doc":"DDC-051","target_page":"39","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"¶ 48","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":74,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-053-6-1-1-cb04a61d","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":6,"target_pdf_page":39,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-053","src_page":"6","text":"Compl. ¶¶ 48, 57","n":"1","kind":"tac","target_doc":"DDC-051","target_page":"44","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"¶ 57","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":75,"k":2,"unit_id":"DDC-053-6-1-2-cb04a61d","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":6,"target_pdf_page":44,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-053","src_page":"7","text":"LCvR 5.4(e)(1)","n":"1","kind":"rule","target_doc":"Local Rules AUG_2025","target_page":"27","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"LCvR 5.4(e)(1)","status":"verified","target_quote":"shall be served, if it is necessary to serve it, by mail or by hand delivery, unless the parties have otherwise agreed","line":76,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-053-7-1-1-69eed61e","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":7,"target_pdf_page":27,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-053","src_page":"7","text":"¶ 21 infra","n":"1","kind":"internal","target_doc":"DDC-053","target_page":"7","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"¶ 21","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":77,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-053-7-1-1-6fd5dcd2","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":7,"target_pdf_page":7,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-053","src_page":"7","text":"Certificate of Service infra","n":"1","kind":"internal","target_doc":"DDC-053","target_page":"8","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"Certificate of Service","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":78,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-053-7-1-1-7da7091c","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":7,"target_pdf_page":8,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-053","src_page":"7","text":"Federal Rule of Civil Procedure 4(i)","n":"1","kind":"rule","target_doc":"Federal Rules of Civil Procedure (Dec. 1, 2025, uscourts.gov official pamphlet)","target_page":"4","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"Rule 4(i)","status":"verified","target_quote":"(1) United States. To serve the United States, a party must: (A)(i) deliver a copy of the summons and of the complaint to the United States attorney for the district where the action is brought-or to an assistant United States attorney or clerical employee whom the United States attorney designates in a writing filed with the court clerk-or (ii) send a copy of each by registered or certified mail to the civil-process clerk at the United States attorney's office; (B) send a copy of each by registered or certified mail to the Attorney General of the United States at Washington, D.C.; and (C) if the action challenges an order of a nonparty agency or officer of the United States, send a copy of each by registered or certified mail to the agency or officer.","line":79,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-053-7-1-1-a3ba21e8","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":7,"target_pdf_page":23,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-053","src_page":"7","text":"LCvR 5.4(e)(1)","n":"2","kind":"rule","target_doc":"Local Rules AUG_2025","target_page":"27","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"LCvR 5.4(e)(1)","status":"verified","target_quote":"(1) Every unsealed document (including an administrative record or a record of state court proceedings) must be filed electronically. Every document filed under seal in a totally sealed case shall be filed in paper form accompanied by an electronic copy in a format deemed compatible by the Clerk's Office with CM/ECF filing in conformity with the requirements of LCvR 5.1. Any document, exhibit, or attachment, including sealed material that (A) is not in a format that readily permits electronic filing, such as a map, chart or DVD, or (B) is illegible when scanned into electronic format, is to be maintained in the possession of the attorney or pro se party responsible for the filing. Such a filing shall be made available for a party or the Court and must be identified in a Notice of Filing filed with the Court. A document or item filed pursuant to this subsection shall be served, if it is necessary to serve it, by mail or by hand delivery, unless the parties have otherwise agreed.","line":80,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-053-7-2-1-69eed61e","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":7,"target_pdf_page":27,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-053","src_page":"8","text":"LCvR 5.4(e)(1)","n":"1","kind":"rule","target_doc":"Local Rules AUG_2025","target_pa